[version]
1.6.6
[date]
2026-10-22
[whatsnew]
- FIXED: Mouse Y coordinate was off by 1 in all windowed apps!
  - Window:resumeMouse() had `relY = y - self.y - 1` (extra -1)
  - The CC:T window at (self.x+1, self.y+1) means:
    relX = sx - self.x, relY = sy - self.y (NO -1!)
  - All mouse clicks were shifted up by 1 row → clicks hit wrong buttons
  - Calculator buttons, editor cursor, file manager selection all broken
  - Now fixed: clicks land exactly where they should
- CHANGED: Terminal commands removed from Apps menu
  - update, print, cleanup, internet, install-to-disk, help, mount,
    hostname, pinestore, pacman are now filtered out
  - Only GUI applications (Terminal, Files, Editor, etc.) appear
  - Terminal commands are still available via the shell
[/whatsnew]
[files]
de/gui.lua
latest_update.upd
[/files]
